# Build context for services/docker/Dockerfile. `cargo build -p inkvec-server` only needs the
# workspace manifests, the crate sources (every member's Cargo.toml must be present for the
# workspace to resolve, even the ones the image does not build) and bindings/openapi.json
# (embedded with include_str!). Everything else here is multi-hundred-MB of benchmark data,
# the WebAssembly demo, docs assets and non-Rust tooling the image never touches.
#
# Deny by default, then allow back only what the build needs.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates
!bindings

# Re-deny within the allowed trees: build artifacts, model weights (never committed; see the
# root .gitignore) and the crates whose own tests/examples pull in large fixtures.
**/target/
crates/inkvec-restore/models/
**/*.onnx
**/*.bpk
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.ckpt
**/*.safetensors
bindings/contract/*.png
bindings/contract/*.rgba
